The first page reviews what the Order 637 FERC Requirements are.
The second page begins a summary of each pipeline’s compliance filings and only includes copies of the ones I have received to date.  These are simply summaries of their filings and will not go into effect until after approval by FERC.

Order 637 FERC Requirements:
Scheduling Equality

Released capacity able to nominate at first opportunity after close of deal
Contract must be issued in one hour
Segmentation

Allowed for capacity holder and release transactions
Explain how tariff complies or make pro forma changes
Allocation policy within the path
Primary points consistent with shippers mainline contract demand
NOT required if total nominations exceed contract demand.
Imbalance Netting & Trading

Imbalance netting and trading must be allowed
Imbalance management services must coincide with imbalance netting & trading
Imbalance Services

Required if pipeline has penalty provisions
Pipeline must permit shippers to obtain imbalance management services from other providers
Imbalance Status

Pipeline must provide timely imbalance and overrun status of each shipper
OFOs 

Tailor OFOs to fit operational parameters of system
Must state pipeline specific standards, objective operational criteria for beginning and ending,    and different levels of system emergencies
Specific operational remedies to be followed prior to OFO
After issuing an OFO, pipeline must report on factors causing issuance and lifting of OFO
Penalties

Justify current penalty provisions against system reliability
Credit penalty and OFO revenues to shippers other than those who incurred them
Crediting details must be provided
Capacity Release and Removal of Price Cap

Removal of maximum price for capacity release transactions until 9/30/02
Capacity release transaction less than 1 year must be posted and bid on during waiver period
Right of First Refusal (ROFR)

ROFR for maximum rate contracts of 12 consecutive months and multi year seasonal contracts

